-          "quote": "Let $U_h\\subset U=L^2(E)$ be the finite-dimensional space of cellwise-constant controls on a finite affine mesh, and let $Q_h=U_h\\cap Q_{ad}$ be nonempty with bounds constant on each control cell. The target is the **exact continuous reduced objective** $\\widehat J$ of [[def-linear-elliptic-pde-constrained-control-problem]], restricted to $Q_h$; write $Ju(q)=c+Sq$ and $g(q)=\\nabla\\widehat J(q)=B^*p(q)+\\alpha q$. Choose a certified $L_h\\ge\\|S|_{U_h}\\|^2+\\alpha>0$. Given a finite budget $N\\ge1$, tolerance $\\tau\\ge0$, and initial $q_0\\in Q_h$, repeat for $k=0,\\ldots,N-1$:\n\n1. Compute conforming finite-element state and adjoint approximations $\\tilde u_k,\\tilde p_k$ and full Strang bounds $\\varepsilon_{u,k},\\varepsilon_{p,k}$ as in [[lem-fem-control-gradient-residual-bound]], including form, geometry, quadrature, and load defects. Set $\\delta_k=\\|B\\|\\varepsilon_{p,k}$ and $\\tilde g_k=B^*\\tilde p_k+\\alpha q_k$.\n2. Set $\\tilde q_{k+1}=P_{Q_h}(q_k-\\tilde g_k/L_h)$, using the clipped-cell-average projection of [[lem-p0-box-projection-is-clipped-cell-average]], and set $\\tilde\\rho_k=\\|q_k-\\tilde q_{k+1}\\|_U$.\n3. If $\\tilde\\rho_k+\\delta_k/L_h\\le\\tau$, return $(q_k,\\texttt{certified},\\tilde\\rho_k+\\delta_k/L_h)$.\n4. Otherwise set $q_{k+1}=\\tilde q_{k+1}$ and continue.\n\nIf all $N$ evaluations finish without that test, return the last evaluated iterate $(q_{N-1},\\texttt{budget-exhausted},\\tilde\\rho_{N-1}+\\delta_{N-1}/L_h)$. A failed or unavailable residual bound returns $(q_k,\\texttt{inconclusive},+\\infty)$. The reported number certifies a projected-gradient residual for the exact continuous PDE objective restricted to $Q_h$; it is not a continuous-control discretization error bound.",
